  "body": "### Description\n\nwhen a user registers on a synapse server and email confirmation is required, the email they receive contains a broken link to an image from matrix.org:\r\n\r\n`<img src=\"https://matrix.org/img/matrix-120x51.png\" width=\"120\" height=\"51\" alt=\"[matrix]\" />`\r\n\r\nshouldn't this be configurable?\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nregister for a new account on a synapse server that requires email confirmation.\r\n\r\nwhen you click on the link to confirm your email you're taken to a page that processes the confirmation, then advises you to close the page and continue in your client.\r\n\r\nthis page refers to a Matrix logo that is not found.\n\n### Homeserver\n\nhttps://synapse.ownyourdata.site/_matrix/static/\n\n### Synapse Version\n\n1.86\n\n### Installation Method\n\nDebian packages from packages.matrix.org\n\n### Database\n\nwhatever default is\n\n### Workers\n\nI don't know\n\n### Platform\n\nubuntu 22\n\n### Configuration\n\nootb\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nthere's no log output but here's a link that should recreate the error:\r\n\r\nhttps://synapse.ownyourdata.site/_matrix/client/unstable/registration/email/submit_token?token=1&client_secret=1&sid=1\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\nnah",
